WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.470
Cuba is a baseball hotbed, but it's patchy
relationship with the United States has long

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:10.079
served as a stumbling block for Cubans hoping
to call Major League Baseball home.

00:00:10.079 --> 00:00:14.440
This looks set to change after Cuba's Baseball
Federation and the "Major League Baseball"

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:21.730
announced a historic deal which could have
widespread diplomatic ramifications.

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:27.330
It's a good day for Cuban baseball, for world
baseball, for our people, for the American

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:29.939
people.

00:00:29.939 --> 00:00:34.440
The agreement should be a home run for both
sides, as it provides Cubans with a safe,

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:39.149
regulated path to playing in the US while
compensating the Cuban Baseball Federation

00:00:39.149 --> 00:00:41.609
for any players making the jump.

00:00:41.609 --> 00:00:46.019
As it currently stands, Cuban players have
to defect and give up their citizenship for

00:00:46.019 --> 00:00:50.660
a chance at making it in the majors, which
has led to criminal organizations trafficking

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:52.280
players.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:58.170
Fans in Havana are pleased with the deal,
if not it's timing.

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:00.649
It's a step forward for the Cuban game.

00:01:00.649 --> 00:01:07.970
It's something the Cuban state should have
done years ago, that's the reality of it.

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:11.900
But political relations could still put the
brakes on the deal.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:16.150
Baseball was an important diplomatic tool
as then-US president Barack Obama sought to

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:20.750
normalize relations with Cuba, and he even
caught a game with Raúl Castro while visiting

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:21.820
Havana.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:25.860
Tensions have reached a higher pitch under
Donald Trump, who has rolled back most of

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:27.740
the agreements made by his predescessor.

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:32.470
US politicans from Trump's Republican party
have already criticized the announced deal.

